\item POSITION TITLE AND REPORTING STRUCTURE

\end{enumerate}

\begin{itemize}

\item Position Title: Senior Software Engineer / Lead Principal Cloud Architect

\item Internal Title (Corporate Org Chart): Lead Principal Cloud Architect, Global Engineering

\item TN Professional Category (USMCA/NAFTA Appendix 2 Schedule): Computer Systems Analyst

\item Department: Global Engineering \& Development

\item Reporting To: Dr. Marcus Chen, Chief Technology Officer (CTO)

\item Employment Type: Full-Time (40 hours per week)

\end{itemize}

\begin{enumerate}

\item START DATE AND REQUESTED EMPLOYMENT DURATION

\end{enumerate}

\begin{itemize}

\item Start Date: August 1, 2026

\item Requested Employment Duration: Three (3) Years (36 Months)

\item End Date: July 31, 2029

\end{itemize}

Immigration Contingency \& Temporary Nature: This employment is temporary in nature and strictly co-terminus with the validity period of your approved non-immigrant visa classification (e.g., TN / O-1A / H-1B). If your visa petition is denied or your authorized stay expires prior to July 31, 2029, your employment with the Company will automatically terminate on the date your legal authorization to work in the United States expires. The Company reserves the right to extend this employment for successive periods upon mutual written agreement and subsequent visa approvals.

\begin{enumerate}

\item ANNUAL SALARY AND COMPENSATION PACKAGE

\end{enumerate}

In recognition of your extraordinary expertise, the Company offers the following highly competitive remuneration package, which meets or exceeds the prevailing wage for this specialty occupation in the San Jose, CA Metropolitan Statistical Area:

\begin{itemize}

\item Annual Base Salary: \$225,000.00 USD per year.

\end{itemize}

(Payable in accordance with the Company’s standard bi-weekly payroll schedule, equating to \$8,653.85 gross per pay period).

\begin{itemize}

\item One-Time Sign-On Bonus: \$50,000.00 USD.

\end{itemize}

(Payable within 30 days of your official Start Date, subject to standard tax withholdings).

\begin{itemize}

\item Annual Target Performance Bonus: Up to 15\% of your base salary (\$33,750.00 USD).

\end{itemize}

(Awarded annually based on the successful delivery of key technical milestones, platform uptime metrics, and individual performance evaluations).

\begin{itemize}

\item Total First-Year Target Cash Compensation: \$308,750.00 USD.

\end{itemize}

Note: This cash compensation is in addition to the Company’s comprehensive executive benefits package, which includes health/dental/vision insurance, a 401(k) retirement plan with company match, and a \$40,000 annual professional development and conference budget.

\begin{enumerate}

\item WORK LOCATION

\end{enumerate}

\begin{itemize}

\item Primary Physical Work Location: Tech Solutions Inc. Headquarters, 100 Innovation Drive, Suite 400, San Jose, CA 95110, USA.

\item Travel Requirements: Occasional domestic and international travel (estimated at 15\% of working time) to attend industry conferences, visit enterprise clients, and collaborate with global engineering teams.

\end{itemize}

\begin{enumerate}

\item SUMMARY OF DUTIES

\end{enumerate}

In your capacity as Lead Principal Cloud Architect, you will perform highly specialized, non-routine duties that require the theoretical and practical application of highly specialized knowledge. Your core responsibilities include:

\begin{itemize}

\item Analyzing the Company's enterprise data-processing and cloud-integration requirements and defining system specifications accordingly.

\item Designing and developing system architecture, including hardware and software configuration specifications for the "DataSync Pro" platform.

\item Evaluating current systems and procedures and recommending modifications to improve efficiency, reliability, and cross-border data synchronization.

\item Preparing detailed system documentation, flowcharts, and technical specifications for engineering and business stakeholders.

\item Testing, troubleshooting, and validating system solutions prior to deployment, and coordinating with engineering staff on implementation.

\end{itemize}

(A comprehensive, detailed Job Description outlining all duties and minimum requirements is attached to this letter as Exhibit A).

